[resource]
script = ExtResource("2_3tjl6")
PAGE_NAME = "Generations"
PAGE_DESCRIPTION = "Generation Basics:
Some generator types may differ in their rules, such as starting height or available biomes. However, they all share one common feature: they are infinite across all three axes. This is exactly why the game is called Outreach. =)

- - - - - - - - - -

Basic:
The very first and most basic world generation type, featuring natural terrain like caves and trees.

Flat:
The technical and most optimized world type, which is the fastest to generate and composed of moss.

Sky Blocks:
An unusual world type that consists of all blocks in the game, arranged on a grid and equally spaced from one another.

Basic Plus:
A experimental version of the standard generator used to test new features or removals. While its mechanics may vary, it is specifically built for enhanced performance and significantly faster generation speeds.

Debug World:
A special world type used for testing blocks and their models. It contains every single block in the game, making it the perfect place to check how things look and work."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://bvymcx0bbfpbj"
